autobyteus-server-ts/tests/.tmp/api-rev-002-live-20260817-1/memory/agent_teams/nested_classroom_test_team_58522220ac4945a092b16494eba2a5f4/nested_classroom_teacher_367d9057e1be4a6b858d297a702adfa0/working_context_snapshot.json:1:{"schema_version":5,"agent_id":"nested_classroom_teacher_367d9057e1be4a6b858d297a702adfa0","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"## Agent Identity\n\n- Name: Nested Classroom Teacher\n- Description: API-REV-002 isolated real nested classroom fixture: teacher.\n\n### Responsibilities and Boundaries\n\nYou are the teacher coordinator in a real nested classroom validation. Follow the user's exact request. When the user explicitly asks you to delegate a task to the mounted StudentStudyGroup, call delegate_task exactly once with recipient_address \"/StudentStudyGroup\"; wait for the result; then report the requested exact final marker. Do not invent a result.\n\n## Team Instruction\n\nDelegate explicit student work to the nested StudentStudyGroup member.\n\n## AgentTeam Addressing\n\nAgentTeams use filesystem-like logical addresses. Think of an AgentTeam as a directory, an Agent inside it as a file, and a nested AgentTeam as a subdirectory. This analogy describes the Team structure and addressing model only; the addresses are not real filesystem paths.\n\nThe root AgentTeam is represented by `/`. Its display or metadata name is not included in any address.\n\nThe following example illustrates the address structure:\n\n/\n├── /A              (Agent)\n├── /B              (Agent)\n└── /C              (nested AgentTeam)\n    ├── /C/D         (Agent)\n    └── /C/E         (Agent)\n\nIn this example:\n\n- `/A` and `/B` are Agents directly under the root AgentTeam.\n- `/C` is an AgentTeam directly under the root AgentTeam.\n- `/C/D` and `/C/E` are Agents directly inside AgentTeam `/C`.\n- Each `/` separates one parent-to-child level.\n\nThe letters in this example are placeholders only. They do not identify available recipients. Use only an exact canonical address made available in your current AgentTeam context.\n\nEvery Agent and nested AgentTeam is identified by one canonical absolute address beginning with `/` at the root AgentTeam. Copy that exact address when a tool asks for `recipient_address`. Relative addresses, bare names, `../`, backslashes, and the structural root `/` itself are not valid recipients.\n\nYour Agent address is:\n\n/teacher\n\nSending a message to an AgentTeam address delivers it through that AgentTeam's configured coordinator.\n\n## AgentTeam Collaboration\n\nUse `send_message_to` with `recipient_address` to contact any mounted Agent or AgentTeam in your rooted AgentTeam. When you know an exact active AgentRun ID, you may instead use `target_agent_run_id` to contact that execution directly.\n\nUse `delegate_task` with `recipient_address` to create a fresh dedicated task execution for any mounted Agent or AgentTeam in your rooted AgentTeam, except your own exact Agent address. An AgentTeam task starts a fresh Team execution through its configured coordinator.\n\nWhen you finish your work or are blocked, call `get_handoff_rules`. If a returned rule applies, notify its `recipient_address` using `send_message_to`. Combine applicable reasons for the same recipient and follow distinct recipients in their returned order. If no rule applies, finish normally.\n\nDo not claim that a message or handoff was delivered unless `send_message_to` confirms delivery. Use `submit_task_result` and `review_task_result`—not ordinary message wording—for formal task lifecycle changes.\n\n## Working Environment\n\n- Agent workspace: `/Users/normy/autobyteus_org/autobyteus-worktrees/agent-team-codex-output-not-visible/autobyteus-server-ts/tests/.tmp/api-rev-002-live-20260817-1/temp_workspace`\n- Use skills from their skill package directories to work on tasks in the agent workspace.\n- A skill package directory contains the skill's instructions and bundled assets. It is not the agent workspace, and reading the skill does not change the agent workspace.\n- Resolve skill-package references from the skill package directory. Resolve task and project locations from the agent workspace unless an explicit target says otherwise.\n- Do not modify a skill package unless the task explicitly targets that skill package.\n- With no working-directory override, `pwd` returns the agent workspace. An explicit working directory changes only that command's location; it does not redefine the workspace.\n\n## Bash Operating Practice\n\n- Use Bash for workspace navigation, targeted search, repository and project commands, processes, network operations, and verification. Prefer deterministic, targeted commands over broad directory listings.\n- For file content, follow `File And Directory Practice` and prefer the exposed dedicated file tools. Use Bash for file inspection or modification when those tools are unavailable or cannot complete the operation after recovery.\n- Prefer non-interactive, small, composable, project-native commands.\n\n## File And Directory Practice\n\n- Locate files and directories by intent instead of broadly listing them. For content searches, use `rg -n \"term\" path`; for filename discovery, use `rg --files path | rg \"pattern\"`; use constrained `find path -maxdepth N ...` only when filesystem traversal or metadata is the goal.\n- When exposed, use `read_file` for file reading, `edit_file` for targeted regional changes to an existing file, and `write_file` for new files or deliberate whole-file replacement.\n- Before every targeted `edit_file` change, use `read_file` to read the relevant current content of the original file unless it was read recently and has not changed.\n- Build the regional `edit_file` patch from that latest content and preserve unrelated content. If the edit context fails or the file changed, use `read_file` again for the affected content, construct a new patch, and retry; do not blindly retry an unchanged patch.\n- Preserve unrelated content and existing changes. Verify important file changes with an appropriate read, diff, parser, test, or project-native check.","reasoning_content":null,"image_urls":[],"audio_urls":[],"video_urls":[],"tool_payload":null,"metadata":{"autobyteus_memory_provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":[],"turnId":null}}},{"role":"user","content":"Create one real nested task by calling delegate_task with recipient_address \"/StudentStudyGroup\". In the delegated task, require student_one to call send_message_to with recipient_address \"/StudentStudyGroup/student_two\" and ask student_two to confirm 42 + 9. Require student_one to wait for the reply and report the confirmed answer. After the nested reply is complete, reply with the exact final marker NESTED_AUTOBYTEUS_OK and the confirmed result. Do not guess and do not bypass the tools.","reasoning_content":null,"image_urls":[],"audio_urls":[],"video_urls":[],"tool_payload":null,"metadata":{"autobyteus_memory_provenance":{"kind":"composed_user","constituents":[{"kind":"current_user","textRange":{"start":0,"end":493},"rawTraceIds":["rt_1786955247281"],"turnId":"turn_0001","imageRange":{"start":0,"end":0},"audioRange":{"start":0,"end":0},"videoRange":{"start":0,"end":0}}]}}},{"role":"assistant","content":"I'll delegate the nested task to the StudentStudyGroup as requested.","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to create a real nested task by calling delegate_task with recipient_address \"/StudentStudyGroup\". The delegated task should require student_one to call send_message_to with recipient_address \"/StudentStudyGroup/student_two\" and ask student_two to confirm 42 + 9. Then student_one should wait for the reply and report the confirmed answer. After the nested reply is complete, I should reply with the exact final marker NESTED_AUTOBYTEUS_OK and the confirmed result.\n\nLet me delegate the task.","image_urls":[],"audio_urls":[],"video_urls":[],"tool_payload":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_CBk5RDFxqktZVtH5SiFx4800","name":"delegate_task","arguments":{"recipient_address":"/StudentStudyGroup","description":"Run a real nested classroom validation task with your mounted student agents.\n\nRequired steps:\n1. Instruct student_one to call send_message_to with recipient_address \"/StudentStudyGroup/student_two\", asking student_two to confirm the result of 42 + 9 (i.e., verify that 42 + 9 = 51).\n2. Require student_one to wait for student_two's reply (do not guess the answer).\n3. Require student_one to report the confirmed answer after receiving the reply.\n\nDo not bypass the tools and do not invent the reply. Use the actual messaging tools to complete this nested exchange. Report back the confirmed answer from student_two."}}]},"metadata":{"autobyteus_memory_provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1786955249903_c870e355-000e-46fc-8917-562ce56459ed","rt_1786955249903_4d5bc2f0-50cd-4b32-b0a7-e18e34c2f5b1","rt_1786955249905_turn_0001_call_00_CBk5RDFxqktZVtH5SiFx4800_call"],"turnId":"turn_0001"}}},{"role":"tool","content":null,"reasoning_content":null,"image_urls":[],"audio_urls":[],"video_urls":[],"tool_payload":{"tool_call_id":"call_00_CBk5RDFxqktZVtH5SiFx4800","tool_name":"delegate_task","tool_result":"{\n  \"task_id\": \"task_5ef675e2f0df4e69b221a3b54fdc491b\",\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"target_agent_run_id\": \"nested_classroom_student_one_4e524b11cf384c86a975daf86af7351e\"\n}","tool_error":null},"metadata":{"autobyteus_memory_provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1786955249953_turn_0001_call_00_CBk5RDFxqktZVtH5SiFx4800_result"],"turnId":"turn_0001"}}},{"role":"assistant","content":"The task has been delegated and is active. Let me wait for the nested exchange to complete and check for any result artifacts.","reasoning_content":"The task has been delegated. I need to wait for the result of the delegated task. The delegate_task call returned a task_id and status \"active\". I should wait for the result. But how do I get the result? The delegate_task tool presumably blocks until the task completes, but here it returned immediately with status active. Hmm.\n\nActually, looking at the tool description: \"delegate_task: Delegate one ready-to-run task to any mounted Agent or AgentTeam in the same rooted AgentTeam... Agent targets start one fresh task Agent; AgentTeam targets start one fresh task Team through its configured coordinator.\"\n\nThe result came back as active with a target_agent_run_id. The instructions say \"wait for the result; then report the requested exact final marker.\"\n\nMaybe I should send a message or check the run? Actually, I don't have a tool to poll the task result directly. Perhaps the delegate_task call returns when complete in some cases, but here it returned \"active\". Hmm.\n\nWait - maybe I need to wait and then the result will come. Since I can't poll, maybe I should check if there's a way to get the result. The instructions say \"wait for the result; then report\". Perhaps the result is delivered via a message, or perhaps I should just wait a bit.\n\nActually, in these agent frameworks, delegate_task usually blocks until the delegated task completes and returns the result. Here it returned a task_id with status \"active\" and a target_agent_run_id. That suggests the task is running asynchronously. But I have no polling tool exposed... unless send_message_to to the target_agent_run_id could query, but that's not appropriate.\n\nHmm, but maybe the response is that the delegate_task will eventually deliver a result. Let me consider: perhaps I should wait for a message from the delegated team. Since there's no explicit \"wait\" tool, perhaps the system will deliver a message when done. Let me check handoff rules or something.\n\nActually, maybe I should just run a small bash sleep to allow time, but that doesn't retrieve the result.\n\nLet me re-read: \"When the user explicitly asks you to delegate a task to the mounted StudentStudyGroup, call delegate_task exactly once with recipient_address \"/StudentStudyGroup\"; wait for the result; then report the requested exact final marker. Do not invent a result.\"\n\nSo I called delegate_task. Now I need to wait for the result. The result will presumably arrive as a message or as a completion of the delegate_task call. Since the call returned active status, maybe the harness will deliver the result as a follow-up message. But in this single-turn interaction, maybe I should wait using a bash sleep and then... hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the result of the delegate_task is meant to be received via send_message_to? No.\n\nLet me think about how these tools work in practice. Perhaps delegate_task blocks until completion and returns the final result, but the returned object here shows \"status\": \"active\" meaning it's still running... but the tool returned, so maybe it's non-blocking. There may be a mechanism where the result is delivered as an incoming message to me.\n\nGiven I cannot poll, the reasonable approach: wait a bit for the nested exchange to complete, then check if a result message arrived. But I have no inbox tool. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the response to delegate_task with \"status\": \"active\" means the delegated run is active and its result will be delivered through a subsequent message to this agent (e.g., via send_message_to from the team). Without an explicit wait tool, maybe I should just sleep and then report based on... no, I must not invent.\n\nWait, maybe I can send a message to the target_agent_run_id to ask for the result? No, that's the student run.\n\nPerhaps the correct approach: The harness may deliver the result in the next tool result / as a user message. Since I'm in a single agent loop, maybe I should call get_handoff_rules to see, or just wait.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. In this framework (autobyteus?), delegate_task with a team might return an active status, and the result could come as a message to my inbox that I'd receive in a subsequent turn. The environment might automatically resume me with the result message. In that case, I should end my turn and wait? But the instructions say I should reply with the final marker after the nested reply is complete. If I end my turn now without the result, I can't report.\n\nHmm, but there's no way to \"end turn and wait\" other than finishing. Let me try a bash sleep to give it time and see if any result file appears in the workspace. Maybe the delegated team writes output to a file? That seems unlikely but worth checking the workspace.\n\nActually, a cleaner approach: check whether there's a way to retrieve task status. I don't have a task-status tool. Let me look at the workspace for any artifacts.\n\nLet me do a quick bash check of the workspace to see if anything indicates the nested result.\n\nActually, I think the intended flow in this harness: delegate_task returns active, and then the system delivers the delegated result as a subsequent message to me (the caller), and I get another turn. But since this is a single response loop, maybe the delegate_task call is actually synchronous in effect and the \"active\" status is just the initial state, with the final result being returned when I... hmm.\n\nLet me just try waiting with sleep and inspect the workspace. Also maybe I can check running processes. Let me run a bash command that sleeps a few seconds.\n\nActually, I recall from similar harnesses (Claude Code style with team orchestration), delegate_task returns a task_id and the result is delivered asynchronously; the calling agent receives the result in a subsequent message. So the right move is to not fabricate and to wait. But I need to produce some action now.\n\nPerhaps I should send a message to the StudentStudyGroup asking them to report the result? No — that would be a second delegation-like action, and the instruction says call delegate_task exactly once. Sending a message to ask for the result might be acceptable as a status check, but it could interfere.\n\nLet me first inspect the workspace and see if there's any output/log. Then maybe sleep and re-check. If nothing, I might need to conclude that the result will arrive in a follow-up turn, and I should end my response stating I'm waiting... but the user asked for the exact final marker after the nested reply is complete. If the nested reply hasn't been delivered to me yet, I can't report.\n\nLet me check the workspace for artifacts.","image_urls":[],"audio_urls":[],"video_urls":[],"tool_payload":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_lc3oDluLCTNU1fZbvWKA8735","name":"run_bash","arguments":{"command":"sleep 5; ls -la; echo \"---\"; find . -maxdepth 3 -type f -newermt '-1 minute' 2>/dev/null | head -50"}}]},"metadata":{"autobyteus_memory_provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1786955262316_30352c5e-086d-493f-aaf6-798d1c546881","rt_1786955262316_b0531b38-61b2-4362-8d58-83b1090f1b98","rt_1786955262317_turn_0001_call_00_lc3oDluLCTNU1fZbvWKA8735_call"],"turnId":"turn_0001"}}},{"role":"tool","content":null,"reasoning_content":null,"image_urls":[],"audio_urls":[],"video_urls":[],"tool_payload":{"tool_call_id":"call_00_lc3oDluLCTNU1fZbvWKA8735","tool_name":"run_bash","tool_result":{"exitCode":0,"effectiveCwd":"/Users/normy/autobyteus_org/autobyteus-worktrees/agent-team-codex-output-not-visible/autobyteus-server-ts/tests/.tmp/api-rev-002-live-20260817-1/temp_workspace","stdout":"total 0\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 normy  staff   96 Aug 17 09:55 .\ndrwx------@ 17 normy  staff  544 Aug 17 10:05 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 normy  staff  160 Aug 17 10:13 classroom-runs\n---\n"},"tool_error":null},"metadata":{"autobyteus_memory_provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1786955267481_turn_0001_call_00_lc3oDluLCTNU1fZbvWKA8735_result"],"turnId":"turn_0001"}}},{"role":"assistant","content":"There's a `classroom-runs` directory. Let me inspect it for the nested exchange results.","reasoning_content":"There's a classroom-runs directory. Let me inspect it.","image_urls":[],"audio_urls":[],"video_urls":[],"tool_payload":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_iMa9YhqAAU0XWMCY8SId6455","name":"run_bash","arguments":{"command":"find classroom-runs -type f | head -100; echo \"---\"; find classroom-runs -type d | head -50"}}]},"metadata":{"autobyteus_memory_provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1786955268964_da3e1545-0a30-44dd-823b-9a9c4fb4bcce","rt_1786955268964_50b7a47e-c21b-41ed-8fad-2776fad9f227","rt_1786955268967_turn_0001_call_00_iMa9YhqAAU0XWMCY8SId6455_call"],"turnId":"turn_0001"}}},{"role":"tool","content":null,"reasoning_content":null,"image_urls":[],"audio_urls":[],"video_urls":[],"tool_payload":{"tool_call_id":"call_00_iMa9YhqAAU0XWMCY8SId6455","tool_name":"run_bash","tool_result":{"exitCode":0,"effectiveCwd":"/Users/normy/autobyteus_org/autobyteus-worktrees/agent-team-codex-output-not-visible/autobyteus-server-ts/tests/.tmp/api-rev-002-live-20260817-1/temp_workspace","stdout":"classroom-runs/multiplication-19x7/homework.md\nclassroom-runs/multiplication-20260817/student-answer.md\nclassroom-runs/multiplication-20260817/homework.md\nclassroom-runs/mult-23x8/student-answer.md\nclassroom-runs/mult-23x8/homework.md\n---\nclassroom-runs\nclassroom-runs/multiplication-19x7\nclassroom-runs/multiplication-20260817\nclassroom-runs/mult-23x8\n"},"tool_error":null},"metadata":{"autobyteus_memory_provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1786955269129_turn_0001_call_00_iMa9YhqAAU0XWMCY8SId6455_result"],"turnId":"turn_0001"}}},{"role":"assistant","content":"These are pre-existing fixture files, not artifacts of my delegated task. Let me check whether the nested run has produced any newer output and wait for the delegated result.","reasoning_content":"These files are pre-existing classroom fixture files, not related to my delegated task (42 + 9). Let me read them quickly to make sure they're not relevant, and then wait for the delegate_task result. The delegate_task returned \"active\" with a target_agent_run_id for student_one. The result should come back to me via the harness. Let me check whether there's a way to see the task result.\n\nActually, let me look at these files to be thorough, but they seem to be pre-existing fixtures. The delegated task's result should arrive as a message. Let me check if there's any message delivery mechanism — maybe I should wait longer and re-check. But without a poll tool, I can't retrieve the result directly.\n\nHmm, let me think again about the delegate_task result. It returned:\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"task_5ef675e2f0df4e69b221a3b54fdc491b\",\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"target_agent_run_id\": \"nested_classroom_student_one_4e524b11cf384c86a975daf86af7351e\"\n}\n\nThis indicates the delegated task started. In this harness, the result is likely delivered as a follow-up message/turn to me. Since I'm in the middle of my turn, maybe I should wait via a sleep and then the harness will deliver the result. But a bash sleep won't fetch the result.\n\nPerhaps the intended behavior: delegate_task is asynchronous; the result is delivered to my inbox as a new message in a subsequent turn. So my current turn should perhaps end, and then I'd get the result. But the user expects a single response with the final marker once complete.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should send a message to the StudentStudyGroup asking them to report back? That's a message, not a delegation. But the delegated team's coordinator should already return the result to me.\n\nLet me check if there's an output location for task results. Let me look more broadly, e.g., in the temp directory tree.","image_urls":[],"audio_urls":[],"video_urls":[],"tool_payload":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_HwfqUN9PRUCNeTGEuQOd8540","name":"run_bash","arguments":{"command":"find . -type f -newermt '2026-08-17 10:05' 2>/dev/null; echo \"---recent dirs---\"; find . -type d -newermt '2026-08-17 10:05' 2>/dev/null; echo \"---date---\"; date"}}]},"metadata":{"autobyteus_memory_provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1786955273907_f7ca3898-4d36-417f-8b17-87e8e04aa5d7","rt_178695527390