he answer.\\n8: 3. State the final numeric answer clearly.\\n9: 4. Reply through `send_message_to` to the professor, and write your answer to the file `student-answer.md` in this same folder:\\n10:    `/Users/normy/autobyteus_org/autobyteus-worktrees/agent-team-codex-output-not-visible/autobyteus-server-ts/tests/.tmp/api-rev-002-live-20260817-1/temp_workspace/classroom-runs/mult-23x8/student-answer.md`\\n11: \\n12: **Expected response format (in `student-answer.md`):**\\n13: - Your name (Student)\\n14: - The problem\\n15: - Your steps\\n16: - The final answer\\n17: \\n18: Return the absolute path to `student-answer.md` in your reply message.\\n\",\"tool_error\":null},\"metadata\":{\"autobyteus_memory_provenance\":{\"kind\":\"single\",\"rawTraceIds\":[\"rt_1786955276655_turn_0001_call_02_dRgtRrsuxGGicWei1llH2594_result\"],\"turnId\":\"turn_0001\"}}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Those are pre-existing fixture files. Let me look for run artifacts related to my delegated task outside the workspace.\",\"reasoning_content\":\"These are pre-existing fixture files unrelated to my delegated 42 + 9 task. They're part of the classroom fixture setup (multiplication homework). My delegated task result should come back through the delegate_task mechanism.\\n\\nThe delegate_task returned status \\\"active\\\" with a target_agent_run_id. I need to wait for the result. Since the harness returns the result asynchronously, perhaps I should wait for a message. But there's no explicit wait tool.\\n\\nHmm, maybe the delegate_task result is delivered when the tool call completes — but it returned \\\"active\\\" immediately. In this environment, the delegated team's coordinator will deliver the result back to me via a message in a subsequent turn.\\n\\nGiven the current turn, perhaps the correct approach is to end my turn, and the result will arrive as a new message. But I cannot \\\"end turn\\\" explicitly — I just produce the final text response. If I produce the final marker now without the result, that would be inventing/guessing, which is forbidden.\\n\\nWait — maybe I should check if there's a message inbox by... there isn't a tool for it.\\n\\nAlternatively, maybe I should send a message to the StudentStudyGroup asking for the result? No — the coordinator will return the result of the delegated task to me automatically.\\n\\nLet me reconsider: maybe delegate_task in this harness is synchronous but the returned payload shows initial status; the actual result may be delivered via a follow-up \\\"assistant message\\\" containing the delegated result. In many of these test harnesses (API-REV style), the delegate_task tool call returns the result when done, OR the result is injected as a new user message with the task result.\\n\\nSince the tool returned immediately with \\\"active\\\", I think the result will be delivered to me as a message. To wait, maybe I can just sleep via bash and then the harness will deliver... no, sleep won't help.\\n\\nActually, let me re-read the delegate_task description: \\\"Delegate one ready-to-run task... Agent targets start one fresh task Agent; AgentTeam targets start one fresh task Team through its configured coordinator.\\\" It doesn't say it blocks until completion. And the return shows status active with target_agent_run_id. So it's async, and the result comes back later, probably as a message to my inbox (which would appear as a new turn in the conversation).\\n\\nIn this situation, the best I can do within this turn is to wait/check for delivery. Since I have no polling tool, perhaps I should simply end my turn with a statement that I'm waiting... but the user asked for the exact final marker after the nested reply is complete. If the nested reply is delivered in a later turn, I'll produce the marker then.\\n\\nBut hold on — maybe I can poll by sleeping in bash for a while and then the harness delivers the result as a tool result? No, that doesn't work.\\n\\nActually, wait. Let me look at this from the harness perspective. The delegate_task returned a result object that included \\\"status\\\": \\\"active\\\". In the autobyteus/agent-team harness, the delegating agent receives the final result as a message (likely via send_message_to from the team coordinator to the caller). The caller then gets it as an incoming message in the next turn.\\n\\nGiven the constraints of this single-turn response, maybe I should wait using repeated sleeps and see if any new files appear in the workspace that the nested team might write. But the nested team was told to use send_message_to, not write files necessarily. Actually, my delegated description didn't ask them to write files.\\n\\nHmm, but actually maybe I misread the environment. Let me check the parent directories for logs or run artifacts, e.g., under tests/.tmp/api-rev-002-live-20260817-1/ there might be more.\",\"image_urls\":[],\"audio_urls\":[],\"video_urls\":[],\"tool_payload\":{\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_00_Nu8CDNGcUY0tGJrTFKNe8870\",\"name\":\"run_bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/normy/autobyteus_org/autobyteus-worktrees/agent-team-codex-output-not-visible/autobyteus-server-ts/tests/.tmp/api-rev-002-live-20260817-1 2>/dev/null && ls -la && echo \\\"---\\\" && find . -maxdepth 3 -newermt '2026-08-17 10:05' -not -path '*/temp_workspace/classroom-runs/*' 2>/dev/null | head -50\"}}]},\"metadata\":{\"autobyteus_memory_provenance\":{\"kind\":\"single\",\"rawTraceIds\":[\"rt_1786955284771_be28c8c0-d2a4-4aea-b0f8-331ea22f780b\",\"rt_1786955284771_778c1418-b1ef-44fb-86ac-da769537e410\",\"rt_1786955284773_turn_0001_call_00_Nu8CDNGcUY0tGJrTFKNe8870_call\"],\"turnId\":\"turn_0001\"}}},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"content\":null,\"reasoning_content\":null,\"image_urls\":[],\"audio_urls\":[],\"video_urls\":[],\"tool_payload\":{\"tool_call_id\":\"call_00_Nu8CDNGcUY0tGJrTFKNe8870\",\"tool_name\":\"run_bash\",\"tool_result\":{\"exitCode\":0,\"effectiveCwd\":\"/Users/normy/autobyteus_org/autobyteus-worktrees/agent-team-co